  "description": [
    {
      "value": "<p>Five years in the canopy of a carbon world, recording nine hundred platforms, their tenure and the arguments about the space between them. The metric survey is still the best in the register and the tenure material is the reason the institute exists at all. The ground control network, however, was established from the canopy on the reasonable assumption that the ground was where it looked to be; it was eleven metres out, and every measurement had to be recomputed. Nobody descended to the forest floor during the entire posting, which the report records without comment.</p>",
